{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-09T01:33:28.349Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"d6e48bfd8a37bc5d501a64ca","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-web-p0me"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Let operators run their own consent manager: storage-notice switch, replay-private regions, sign-in analytics events"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Operators who run an opt-in consent manager at their reverse proxy see two banners today, and the built-in storage notice claims no optional tracking exists, which is wrong for such deployments. pm-web also renders private project, item and account data that must stay out of session-replay tools by default, and sign-in starts are invisible to analytics."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["privacy;analytics;consent;operator-config"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-09T01:33:28.349Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-09T01:33:28.349Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"PM_WEB_STORAGE_NOTICE=on|off server setting (default on) documented in the README configuration table; GET /api/ui-config returns {storageNotice:boolean}; With off, cookie-consent.js never shows the notice, never writes pm_cookie_preferences_v1, and data-cookie-settings buttons fall back to a plain link to the operator's cookie-settings legal page; with on behaviour is unchanged; fetch failure falls back to on without throwing; Every private-content container (#main-app, #modal-container, #toast-container, #live-copy-announcement) and dynamically created private overlays carry data-umami-block; the sign-in screen stays unblocked; a test fails if any listed container loses the attribute; Sign-in buttons carry data-umami-event auth_sign_in_started with provider password / oidc; no user name, e-mail or token in any attribute; privacy-policy.html template tells operators running an analytics or consent manager to describe it and explains PM_WEB_STORAGE_NOTICE=off; no visitor-visible vendor names anywhere; Tests cover both setting values over real HTTP and the client script over the built artifact; focused tests, typecheck and lint pass locally"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"6a2fd9c722eed81ffd1bd458c57a835f799761d1993bcde501fc497911fb1899","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"3de1bd582a56cdfbcdd99b88a8696dde131f56027c47b96a598b990a9ffe790f"}
